   "box": 1,
   "kind_hint": "management",
   "section": "Manage and refer urgently:",
   "section_y": 172.9,
   "indent": 1,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Do ECG if available and send with patient.",
   "bbox": [
    51.2,
    203.1,
    218.1,
    213.9
   ],
   "key": "p26-2771df4c"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-rb1-e17",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 1,
   "kind_hint": "management",
   "section": "Manage and refer urgently:",
   "section_y": 172.9,
   "indent": 1,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "If chest pain, confusion, BP < 90/60 or signs of heart failure, or stroke: discuss with specialist if immediate treatment or cardioversion needed before urgent referral.",
   "bbox": [
    51.2,
    213.1,
    677.6,
    223.9
   ],
   "key": "p26-2cdfc9ef"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-out-e01",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Palpitations refer to patient's unpleasant awareness of his/her own fast or irregular heartbeat. Patient may describe 'heart racing’ or 'pounding’ or 'fluttering in the chest’.",
   "bbox": [
    114.1,
    89.5,
    729.8,
    99.7
   ],
   "key": "p26-3c301571"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-out-e02",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Review in 2 days. If palpitations persist, refer for further assessment.",
   "bbox": [
    285.0,
    513.4,
    557.1,
    524.6
   ],
   "key": "p26-bf4aaad8"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-out-e03",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "1Consult the South African Medicines Formulary (SAMF) or MIC helpline. 2Medications that prolong QT interval: macrolides (azithromycin), fluoroquinolones (moxifloxacin), bedaquiline, antipsychotics (haloperidol), antidepressants (citalopram or amitriptyline).",
   "bbox": [
    34.0,
    535.3,
    778.8,
    551.8
   ],
   "key": "p26-86554096"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-out-e04",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "PALPITATIONS",
   "bbox": [
    362.7,
    48.7,
    480.8,
    71.0
   ],
   "key": "p26-69890eed"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-out-e05",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Approach to the patient with palpitations not needing urgent attention • If any of the following, arrange for cardiology appointment, same week if possible: known current or previous heart disease, a history of fainting, or family history of sudden death. • Also do an ECG (if available) and discuss/refer to doctor for review. If unsure whether ECG is abnormal, discuss with specialist.",
   "bbox": [
    76.5,
    242.1,
    735.7,
    273.3
   ],
   "key": "p26-6438e9f2"
  },
  {
   "id": "p26-out-e06",
   "page": 26,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Sinus rhythm",
   "bbox": [
    495.9,
    287.1,
    544.2,
    297.3
   ],
   "key": "p26-970e558c"
  },
